                  "mes25":1,"mes26":1,"mes27":1,"mes28":1,"mes29":1,"mes30":1}
      }
    },
    "report": {
      "template": "standard",
      "include": ["timestamp", "completion_time", "dimension_scores"],
      "header": "Moral Expansiveness Scale (MES) Report",
      "footer_refs": [
        "Crimston, D., Bain, P. G., Hornsey, M. J., & Bastian, B. (2016). Moral expansiveness: Examining variability in the capacity to include others in the moral circle. Journal of Personality and Social Psychology, 111(4), 636–653. https://doi.org/10.1037/pspp0000086",
        "Scoring: each entity placed into Inner Circle = 3, Outer Circle = 2, Fringes = 1, Outside = 0. Subscales: Humans (items 1–18, range 0–54), Animals (19–24, range 0–18), Nature (25–30, range 0–18), Total (0–90)."
      ]
    }
  },
  "translations": {
    "en": {
      "mes_head": "For each entity below, please indicate your level of moral concern by selecting the category that best reflects where you would place it.",
      "mes_r1": "Inner Circle of Moral Concern",
      "mes_r2": "Outer Circle of Moral Concern",
      "mes_r3": "Fringes of Moral Concern",
      "mes_r4": "Outside the Moral Boundary",
